# CompTIA A+ — Operational Procedures

Which tool protects components from ESD while you work inside a case?
---
anti-static wrist strap
= antistatic wrist strap
= anti-static strap
= ESD strap
= wrist strap
---
Clip it to unpainted chassis metal. Parts in transit go in anti-static bags.

Which environmental condition increases the risk of ESD?
---
low humidity
= dry air
= low humidity levels
---
Dry air builds static charge. Very high humidity risks condensation instead.

Which component stores dangerous voltage even when unplugged?
---
Power supply
~ RAM stick
~ NVMe SSD
~ CMOS battery
---
Its capacitors hold charge after power-off. CRT monitors and laser printer fusers are the other classic keep-out zones.

Which file extension is a PowerShell script?
---
.ps1
= ps1
---
.bat is the old cmd.exe batch language. .vbs is VBScript.

Which file extension is a Windows batch file?
---
.bat
= bat
---
Runs in cmd.exe. PowerShell scripts use .ps1.

Which file extension is a Linux shell script?
---
.sh
= sh
---
Needs execute permission first: chmod +x.

Which file extension is a Python script?
---
.py
= py
---
Cross-platform, but the interpreter must be installed.

Which backup type copies everything regardless of when it last changed?
---
full
= full backup
---
Slowest to make, fastest to restore.

Which backup type copies only what changed since the last backup of any kind?
---
incremental
= incremental backup
---
Fast to make, but a restore needs the full plus every incremental since.

Which backup type copies everything changed since the last full backup?
---
differential
= differential backup
---
A restore needs just the full plus the latest differential.

What does the 3-2-1 backup rule call for?
---
3 copies on 2 different media with 1 offsite
~ 3 backups a day, 2 of them verified, 1 archived
~ 3 drives split into 2 partitions and 1 folder
~ 3 fulls, 2 incrementals, 1 differential
---
The offsite copy survives fire and theft. Cloud storage counts as offsite.
